    "query_text": "Human T-lymphotropic virus type-I-associated myelopathy / tropical spastic paraparesis (HAM/TSP) patients produce Immunoglobulin G (IgG) antibodies which cross-react with an immunodominant epitope in Tax.",
    "reference_answer": "HAM/TSP patients produce IgG antibodies that cross‑react with an immunodominant epitope in the HTLV‑1 Tax protein.",
    "model_answer": "The provided documents do not contain enough evidence to confirm that HAM/TSP patients produce Immunoglobulin G (IgG) antibodies which cross-react with an immunodominant epitope in Tax. \n\nAlthough Document 1 mentions that antibodies to hnRNP-A1 cross-reacted with HTLV-1-tax, it does not specifically state that these are IgG antibodies. Therefore, the",
    "selected_doc_ids": "[\"5476778\", \"23326722\", \"44420873\"]",
