    "model_answer": "The evidence is insufficient to confirm that during the primary early antibody response, activated B cells migrate toward the inner-and outer paracortical areas where oxysterol accumulation is generated by stromal cells. \n\nWhile Document 1 discusses B-cell migration in the early phases of T-dependent antibody responses and the role of chemokines and receptors in guiding B cells to specific niches, it does not mention",
